⭐ PART 1 — Steam + Starfield Player Gallery Guide
This is written for regular players, not engineers.
It’s friendly, clear, and explains exactly how SIG works behind the scenes.

⭐ THE STARFIELD INTELLIGENT GALLERY — PLAYER GUIDE
Steam Recordings + Starfield Captures + SIG Automation
🎮 What SIG Does Automatically
When you turn on SIG’s Steam Automation feature, SIG quietly runs a tiny background process that:

Detects new Steam game recordings

Converts them into MP4 videos

Imports them into your Gallery

Generates thumbnails

Stores metadata

Prepares them for cinematic playback

This happens even when SIG is closed.

You don’t have to drag files, convert formats, or hunt through folders.
SIG does the work for you.

🎥 How to Record Gameplay in Steam
Starfield uses Steam’s built‑in recording system.

To start recording:
Press:

Code
ALT + F10
To stop recording:
Press:

Code
ALT + F10
again.

Steam will save your recording automatically.

SIG will detect it within 5 seconds.

🗂️ Where Steam Stores Recordings
Steam stores recordings inside your Steam “userdata” folder.

SIG automatically finds this folder — you don’t need to know where it is.

🌌 How SIG Uses Starfield
SIG automatically detects your Starfield installation so it can:

read Starfield captures

link videos to your Starfield journey

prepare Temple and Artifact sequences

build your personal Starfield timeline

You don’t need to configure anything.

🧒 Parent / Caregiver Controls
Inside:

Code
C:\SIG\Settings\steam_auto_ingest.json
You’ll find:

json
{
    "auto_ingest_enabled": true
}
Set this to false to disable background ingestion.

SIG will stop listening for new recordings until you turn it back on.

⭐ That’s it.
SIG is designed to be:

simple

automatic

invisible

magical

You play Starfield.
SIG remembers your journey.